{
 "thread": "a8ZFyyILWvo",
 "subject": "Adapting to new release",
 "messages_listed": 4,
 "last_activity": "2012-09-10T19:22:45Z",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "Dtm5r-cF6wkJ",
   "from": "Dianne Cook",
   "author": "43d45a846d16a3b9",
   "date": "2012-09-07T15:08:21Z",
   "subject": "Adapting to new release",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div>I used these functions to get the text for the tick marks of an axis in the previous version of ggplot2. It now throws an error about gTree. Anybody know what the best way to get the axis tick labels with the new version??</div><div><br></div><div>    #pGrob &lt;- ggplotGrob(p)</div><div>    #axisBreaks &lt;- as.numeric(getGrob(pGrob, &quot;axis.text.x&quot;, grep = TRUE)$label)</div><div><br></div><div>cheers,</div><div>Di</div><div><br></div><div>\r\n<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><span style=\"font-size:12px\">---------------------------</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12px\"></span>Di Cook</div><div><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">vis...@gmail.com</a></div><div><br></div></div><br><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "L7tnplDBcqUJ",
   "from": "Brandon Hurr",
   "author": "27405c4b711a1080",
   "date": "2012-09-07T15:17:57Z",
   "subject": "Re: Adapting to new release",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "There&#39;s a discussion on the development list about how to access elements within the grob table. Apparently 0.92 breaks the ability to call it by name. <div><br></div><div>Dennis Murphy is working on a transition guide for the new themeing system in 0.92, but in the meantime some of the devs should be able to help. </div>\r\n\r\n<div><br></div><div>Below is a copy of that email, which might help you with your problem. Sadly, I have no experience with messing with Grobs. </div><div><br></div><div>B<br><br></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">Hi everyone -</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">A couple questions on the main ggplot2 mailing list have gotten me</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">thinking about how to access grobs in gtable objects. I&#39;m looking for</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">some feedback about how to go about doing this.</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">As you may know, ggplot now generates a gtable object. Here&#39;s an</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">example of how to access and view a gtable:</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">library(ggplot2)</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">library(grid)</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">p &lt;- qplot(1:3, 1:3, colour=c(&quot;a&quot;, &quot;b&quot;, &quot;c&quot;))</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"># Generate the gtable grob</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">g &lt;- ggplotGrob(p)</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"># display it</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">grid.newpage()</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">grid.draw(g)</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"># Print gtable</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">g</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"># TableGrob (6 x 6) &quot;layout&quot;: 9 grobs</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">#   (1-6,1-6) background: rect[plot.background.rect.489]</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">#   (4-4,3-3) spacer: absoluteGrob[GRID.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">absoluteGrob.462]</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">#   (3-3,4-4) panel: zeroGrob[NULL]</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">#   (3-3,3-3) axis-l: gTree[GRID.gTree.450]</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">#   (4-4,4-4) axis-b: absoluteGrob[GRID.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">absoluteGrob.456]</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">#   (5-5,4-4) xlab: text[axis.title.x.text.464]</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">#   (3-3,2-2) ylab: text[axis.title.y.text.466]</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">#   (3-3,5-5) guide-box: gtable[guide-box]</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">#   (2-2,4-4) title: text[plot.title.text.487]</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"># Layout information is stored in the data frame &#39;layout&#39;</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">g$layout</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">#   t l b r z clip       name</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"># 9 1 1 6 6 0   on background</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"># 1 3 3 3 3 3  off     axis-l</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"># 2 4 3 4 3 1  off     spacer</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"># 3 3 4 3 4 2   on      panel</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"># 4 4 4 4 4 4  off     axis-b</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"># 5 5 4 5 4 5  off       xlab</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"># 6 3 2 3 2 6  off       ylab</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"># 7 3 5 3 5 7  off  guide-box</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"># 8 2 4 2 4 8  off      title</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"># Access a single grob -- this will get the first one listed in the table</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">g$grobs[[1]]</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"># rect[plot.background.rect.489]</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">As you can see, when you print the gtable object, it displays the name</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">(taken from the &#39;layout&#39; column in the data frame) followed by the</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">type of grob, and finally the grob name (in square brackets). For</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">example, the first entry in the table is named in the gtable layout</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">&quot;background&quot;, but the name of the grob is &quot;plot.background.rec.489&quot;.</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">I&#39;ll call these the layoutName and grobName, respectively. The</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">layoutName is something used by gtable; the grobName is a property of</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">the grob itself.</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">Previously the grobs had grobNames like &quot;background&quot;, &quot;axis-l&quot;, and so</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">on. These are now used as the layoutNames, and the grobNames generally</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">aren&#39;t nice and simple like this.</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">Here are a couple things that seem to be more difficult now:</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">- I don&#39;t think there&#39;s a simple way of accessing the grobs by name.</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">- </span><a href=\"http://grid.ls/\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://grid.ls/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792374739952000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2946zHN0Rz6tc4_j4Xbrw_\">grid.ls</a><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">() no longer produces a nice tree of the grob hierarchy.</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">Any thoughts on how these things could be improved, and what else</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">could be improved? There may be some other things I&#39;m missing -- feel</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.800000190734863px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">free to chime in.</span><br>\r\n<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Fri, Sep 7, 2012 at 4:08 PM, Dianne Cook <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">vis...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n\r\n<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div>I used these functions to get the text for the tick marks of an axis in the previous version of ggplot2. It now throws an error about gTree. Anybody know what the best way to get the axis tick labels with the new version??</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<div><br></div><div>    #pGrob &lt;- ggplotGrob(p)</div><div>    #axisBreaks &lt;- as.numeric(getGrob(pGrob, &quot;axis.text.x&quot;, grep = TRUE)$label)</div><div><br></div><div>cheers,</div><div>Di</div><div><br></div>\r\n\r\n<div>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><span style=\"font-size:12px\">---------------------------</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12px\"></span>Di Cook</div><div><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">vis...@gmail.com</a></div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<span><font color=\"#888888\"><div><br></div></font></span></div><span><font color=\"#888888\"><br><br>\r\n</font></span></div><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n<br></font></span></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the ggplot2 mailing list.<br>\r\nPlease provide a reproducible example: <a href=\"https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792374739952000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3onr5eYE0om22rIv2QcSzg\">https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility</a><br>\r\n <br>\r\nTo post: email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\nTo unsubscribe: email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggplot2+u...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\nMore options: <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792374739953000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1RXsnKUio8xbJczY2F5YT7\">http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2</a><br>\r\n</font></span></blockquote></div><br></div>\r\n"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "-xwGBpkHtsQJ",
   "from": "Winston Chang",
   "author": "d34d025a513c07fc",
   "date": "2012-09-08T05:13:48Z",
   "subject": "Re: Adapting to new release",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div>Retrieving it from the ggplot grob is much more complicated now, because of the lack of easy accessor functions in the new gtable structure used by ggplot. It&#39;s possible, but ugly. The hard thing about getting the scale breaks is that they&#39;re not computed until the ggplot object is rendered, which probably why you had to extract it from the grob in the past.</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<div><br></div><div>You can get similar information is to create a scale and train it on your data. For example, this will create a continuous x scale object, train it on the values 1:10, and then retrieve information about the breaks, labels, and range.</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<div><div><br></div><div>sc &lt;- scale_x_continuous()</div><div>scale_train_df(sc, data.frame(x = 1:10))</div><div>ggplot2:::scale_break_info(sc)</div></div><div><br></div><div>This can be done without even creating a ggplot object. The drawback is that if your plot has stats that modify the data, then the breaks won&#39;t match what you get here.</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>If you must get the labels from the grob, here&#39;s some code that does that. Like I said before, it&#39;s ugly:</div><div><div># Create a grob from ggplot</div><div>p &lt;- qplot(1:3, 1:3, colour=1:3)</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<div>g &lt;- ggplotGrob(p)</div></div><div><br></div><div><div># Print the layout.</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div><div>g$layout</div><div>#   t l b r z clip       name</div><div># 9 1 1 6 6 0   on background</div><div># 1 3 3 3 3 3  off     axis-l</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<div># 2 4 3 4 3 1  off     spacer</div><div># 3 3 4 3 4 2   on      panel</div><div># 4 4 4 4 4 4  off     axis-b</div><div># 5 5 4 5 4 5  off       xlab</div><div># 6 3 2 3 2 6  off       ylab</div><div># 7 3 5 3 5 7  off  guide-box</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<div># 8 2 4 2 4 8  off      title</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div></div><div><br></div><div><div># Here&#39;s a simple accessor functions for the grobs:</div><div>gt_getgrob &lt;- function(gt, pattern) {</div><div>  idx &lt;- grep(pattern, gt$layout$name)</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<div>  if (length(idx) &gt; 1)</div><div>    stop(&quot;More than one match for pattern &#39;&quot;, pattern, &quot;&#39;&quot;)</div><div><br></div><div>  gt$grobs[[idx]]</div><div>}</div></div><div><br></div><div><br></div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<div><div># Get each of the axes</div><div>axis_l &lt;- gt_getgrob(g, &quot;axis-l&quot;)</div><div>axis_b &lt;- gt_getgrob(g, &quot;axis-b&quot;)</div><div><br></div><div># Draw them</div><div>grid.newpage()</div><div>grid.draw(axis_l)</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<div>grid.draw(axis_b)</div></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><div># Extract the labels</div><div>axis_l$children[[2]]$grobs[[1]]$label</div><div><div>axis_r$children[[2]]$grobs[[2]]$label</div></div><div><br></div>\r\n\r\n<div><br></div><div>-Winston</div><div><br></div>\r\n<div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<br>On Friday, September 7, 2012, Dianne Cook  wrote:<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div>I used these functions to get the text for the tick marks of an axis in the previous version of ggplot2. It now throws an error about gTree. Anybody know what the best way to get the axis tick labels with the new version??</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<div><br></div><div>    #pGrob &lt;- ggplotGrob(p)</div><div>    #axisBreaks &lt;- as.numeric(getGrob(pGrob, &quot;axis.text.x&quot;, grep = TRUE)$label)</div><div><br></div><div>cheers,</div><div>Di</div><div><br></div>\r\n\r\n<div>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><span style=\"font-size:12px\">---------------------------</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12px\"></span>Di Cook</div><div><a rel=\"nofollow\">vis...@gmail.com</a></div>\r\n<div><br></div></div><br><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<br></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the ggplot2 mailing list.<br>\r\nPlease provide a reproducible example: <a href=\"https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792374739954000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0mdJGq-cXkysNZIH_rYn_d\">https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility</a><br>\r\n <br>\r\nTo post: email <a rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\nTo unsubscribe: email <a rel=\"nofollow\">ggplot2+u...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\nMore options: <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792374739954000&amp;usg=AOvVaw31RiOqVjuE6ta5TXvQ7IFP\">http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2</a><br>\r\n</blockquote>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "qRbsWJCvUlcJ",
   "from": "Winston Chang",
   "author": "d34d025a513c07fc",
   "date": "2012-09-10T19:22:45Z",
   "subject": "Re: Adapting to new release",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "I thought I&#39;d pass this along to the list... In another email, Hadley pointed out a better way to get the break information:<div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-size:13px;font-family:arial,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-size:13px;font-family:arial,sans-serif\">p &lt;- qplot(1:3, 1:3, colour=c(&quot;a&quot;, &quot;b&quot;, &quot;c&quot;))</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-size:13px;font-family:arial,sans-serif\">\r\n\r\n\r\n</div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-size:13px;font-family:arial,sans-serif\">print(p)$panel$ranges</span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-size:13px;font-family:arial,sans-serif\">\r\n<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_quote\">-Winston</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Sat, Sep 8, 2012 at 12:13 AM, Winston Chang <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">winsto...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br>\r\n\r\n\r\n<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div>Retrieving it from the ggplot grob is much more complicated now, because of the lack of easy accessor functions in the new gtable structure used by ggplot. It&#39;s possible, but ugly. The hard thing about getting the scale breaks is that they&#39;re not computed until the ggplot object is rendered, which probably why you had to extract it from the grob in the past.</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div><br></div><div>You can get similar information is to create a scale and train it on your data. For example, this will create a continuous x scale object, train it on the values 1:10, and then retrieve information about the breaks, labels, and range.</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div><div><br></div><div>sc &lt;- scale_x_continuous()</div><div>scale_train_df(sc, data.frame(x = 1:10))</div><div>ggplot2:::scale_break_info(sc)</div></div><div><br></div><div>This can be done without even creating a ggplot object. The drawback is that if your plot has stats that modify the data, then the breaks won&#39;t match what you get here.</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>If you must get the labels from the grob, here&#39;s some code that does that. Like I said before, it&#39;s ugly:</div><div><div># Create a grob from ggplot</div><div>p &lt;- qplot(1:3, 1:3, colour=1:3)</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div>g &lt;- ggplotGrob(p)</div></div><div><br></div><div><div># Print the layout.</div><div><div>g$layout</div><div>#   t l b r z clip       name</div><div># 9 1 1 6 6 0   on background</div><div># 1 3 3 3 3 3  off     axis-l</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div># 2 4 3 4 3 1  off     spacer</div><div># 3 3 4 3 4 2   on      panel</div><div># 4 4 4 4 4 4  off     axis-b</div><div># 5 5 4 5 4 5  off       xlab</div><div># 6 3 2 3 2 6  off       ylab</div><div># 7 3 5 3 5 7  off  guide-box</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div># 8 2 4 2 4 8  off      title</div></div></div><div><br></div><div><div># Here&#39;s a simple accessor functions for the grobs:</div><div>gt_getgrob &lt;- function(gt, pattern) {</div><div>  idx &lt;- grep(pattern, gt$layout$name)</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div>  if (length(idx) &gt; 1)</div><div>    stop(&quot;More than one match for pattern &#39;&quot;, pattern, &quot;&#39;&quot;)</div><div><br></div><div>  gt$grobs[[idx]]</div><div>}</div></div><div><br></div><div><br></div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div><div># Get each of the axes</div><div>axis_l &lt;- gt_getgrob(g, &quot;axis-l&quot;)</div><div>axis_b &lt;- gt_getgrob(g, &quot;axis-b&quot;)</div><div><br></div><div># Draw them</div><div>grid.newpage()</div><div>grid.draw(axis_l)</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div>grid.draw(axis_b)</div></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><div># Extract the labels</div><div>axis_l$children[[2]]$grobs[[1]]$label</div><div><div>axis_r$children[[2]]$grobs[[2]]$label</div></div><span><font color=\"#888888\"><div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<br></div>\r\n<div><br></div><div>-Winston</div><div><br></div>\r\n<div><br></div></font></span></div><div><div><br>On Friday, September 7, 2012, Dianne Cook  wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div>I used these functions to get the text for the tick marks of an axis in the previous version of ggplot2. It now throws an error about gTree. Anybody know what the best way to get the axis tick labels with the new version??</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div><br></div><div>    #pGrob &lt;- ggplotGrob(p)</div><div>    #axisBreaks &lt;- as.numeric(getGrob(pGrob, &quot;axis.text.x&quot;, grep = TRUE)$label)</div><div><br></div><div>cheers,</div><div>Di</div><div><br></div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><span style=\"font-size:12px\">---------------------------</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12px\"></span>Di Cook</div><div><a rel=\"nofollow\">vis...@gmail.com</a></div>\r\n<div><br></div></div><br><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<br></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the ggplot2 mailing list.<br>\r\nPlease provide a reproducible example: <a href=\"https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792374739956000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2-tg7EqR0vPfE3eHfKC9qw\">https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility</a><br>\r\n <br>\r\nTo post: email <a rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\nTo unsubscribe: email <a rel=\"nofollow\">ggplot2+u...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\nMore options: <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792374739957000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0BEMM0YGcohoC1RYqXG6JM\">http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2</a><br>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n</div></div></blockquote></div><br></div>"
    ]
